# DESK38 -- *Show info* on the DESKTOP surface: the drive icon, the trash and
# the printer.  Before DESK38 `do_info_rename` returned at once for
# `G.g_cwin == DESKWH`, so all three did nothing at all.
#
#   B_CSEL      the C: drive icon selected
#   C_DISKINFO  the ADDISKIN box (drive letter, label, folders, files, bytes
#               used, bytes available)
#   D_TRASH     the trash selected
#   E_TRASHINFO the STTRINFO alert ("... is used to permanently delete files")
#   F_PRINTER   the printer selected
#   G_PRNTINFO  the STPRINFO alert ("... is a printer.")
#
# Coordinates, all from the probe run of this measurement:
#   desk obj  9 (C:)      click (38,35)
#   desk obj 10 (TRASH)   click (38,449)
#   desk obj 11 (PRINTER) click (584,449)
#   File title hover (88,9); "Info/Rename..." click (152,43)
# The two alert OK buttons and the ADDISKIN OK button are filled in from this
# run's own [alert]/[dlg] dumps -- the first pass (d38a-probe) only reaches
# C_DISKINFO and stops there.
100 parkbr
300 move 600 240
1000 arm
1200 mark A_IDLE
1600 move 38 35
2000 down
2003 up
2400 parkbr
3000 mark B_CSEL
3400 move 88 240
3600 move 88 9
4200 move 152 43
4800 down
5000 up
5600 parkbr
7000 mark C_DISKINFO
# -- second pass: OK the disk box (245,334 from this run's [dlg] dump), then
#    select the trash and ask again, to measure the STTRINFO alert.
7400 move 245 334
7800 down
8000 up
8600 parkbr
9400 mark D_DISKOK
9800 move 38 449
10200 down
10203 up
10600 parkbr
11200 mark E_TRASHSEL
11600 move 88 240
11800 move 88 9
12400 move 152 43
13000 down
13200 up
13800 parkbr
14600 mark F_TRASHINFO
# -- third pass: OK the trash alert (320,277 from this run's [alert] dump),
#    then the printer.
15000 move 320 277
15400 down
15600 up
16200 parkbr
17000 mark G_TRASHOK
17400 move 584 449
17800 down
17803 up
18200 parkbr
18800 mark H_PRNTSEL
19200 move 88 240
19400 move 88 9
20000 move 152 43
20600 down
20800 up
21400 parkbr
22200 mark I_PRNTINFO
